# What must not enter the build context for deployment/frontend/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` beside the Dockerfile in preference to a `.dockerignore`
# at the root of the context, which is why this lives here.
#
# ## `**/node_modules/`, not `node_modules/`
#
# The pattern is anchored at the context root. `node_modules/` alone therefore excludes exactly one
# directory — the repository's own — and lets `frontend/node_modules` through, which is the one that
# matters: it is the largest directory in the tree, and `COPY frontend/ ./` drops it straight on top
# of the `node_modules` the image just installed. pnpm's store is content-addressed with absolute
# symlinks into the developer's home directory, so what lands in the image is thousands of links
# pointing at paths that do not exist there. The symptom is not a missing file: `pnpm exec` decides
# the dependency tree is out of date and re-runs `pnpm install`, which fails inside a build that
# already installed everything correctly.
#
# `deployment/quickstart/Dockerfile.dockerignore` used to have the anchored form and the same latent
# problem; it was fixed when the release image started building the interface, and again when it
# stopped.
**/node_modules/

# Build output. `out/` is a full Mill tree and is routinely gigabytes; the rest is this build's own
# product, and copying a previous run's output in is how a stale artefact ships.
out/
frontend/dist/
frontend/storybook-static/
**/target/

# Version control and editor state: large, and none of it changes what is built.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.bsp/
.metals/
.bloop/

# Everything the browser build does not read. The bundle is built from `frontend/packages` alone, so
# none of the Scala tree is an input — and leaving it out means an unrelated backend edit does not
# invalidate this image's cache.
libs/
services/
apps/
e2e/
build-tests/
docs/
research/

# `deployment/` is *not* excluded wholesale any more: this image copies its own entrypoint out of
# it. Excluding the directory and then `COPY deployment/frontend/entrypoint.sh` is a build that
# fails with "not found" on a file that is plainly there, which is a confusing ten minutes.
deployment/compose/
deployment/demo/
deployment/quickstart/
deployment/secured/
deployment/storybook/

**/*.log
